  SEC filings are works of the United States government and are in the public
  domain, so committing a real excerpt is fine. This one is cut down to the
  elements data/etf_holdings.py actually parses:

    headerData/filerInfo/seriesClassInfo/seriesId  -> series disambiguation
    formData/genInfo/repPdEnd, repPdDate           -> the PIT anchor
    formData/invstOrSecs/invstOrSec/*              -> the basket

  The positions are deliberately heterogeneous so the parser's honesty
  contracts are exercised by the fixture itself:

    AAPL  — complete row (pctVal + units=NS + balance)
    MSFT  — complete row
    NVDA  — no pctVal            => weight NaN, never 0.0 (CONSTRAINT #4)
    AMZN  — units=PA (principal) => shares_held NaN, not a mis-scaled count
    (last) — no <ticker> at all  => skipped entirely, never keyed by CUSIP
-->
